# Pairs with RetainedRestorable. The increment re-checks its base by reading
# the base's sink manifest - the read it already made before draining - rather
# than its catalog row. A pass removes the row first and the sink manifest
# only after its scan, so a check between the two passes while the scan has
# already missed the increment, and the pass deletes a published increment's
# base.
MODULE: RetainedRestorableCheckReadsSinkManifest
TARGET: RetainedRestorable
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the base re-check reads the sink manifest instead of the catalog row
PERTURBS: Check

--- FIND
                    IF m.kind = "full" \/ m.base \in cat THEN "ok" ELSE "abandon"]
--- REPLACE
                    \* MUTATION: the check reads the base's sink manifest.
                    IF m.kind = "full" \/ m.base \in snk THEN "ok" ELSE "abandon"]
--- END